{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>He is Edom.</b> Scripture says this three times in this parashah. Since HaShem swore to destroy Edom, therefore it mentions concerning Esav that he is Edom, and it mentions the city, as it is written (Genesis 36:8): ״בְּהַר שֵׂעִיר הוּא אֱדוֹם״ — if this does not apply to Esav, apply it to the city itself. And it mentions the sons of Esav that they are Edom, as it is written (Genesis 36:19): ״וְאֵלֶּה אַלּוּפֵיהֶם הוּא אֱדוֹם״ — to say that all of them will be kindled in the fire of the house of Jacob, since all of them are called Edom, which HaShem gave to Israel, and also Esav himself. This is alluded to in the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory (Tanhuma, Tzav; Yerushalmi Nedarim 3:5), who said: In the future Esav will wrap himself in tzitzit and come and sit among the righteous, and the Holy One, blessed be He, will pull him away from there, etc., as it is written (Obadiah 1:4): ״וְאִם בֵּין כּוֹכָבִים וְגוֹ׳ מִשָּׁם״ וְגוֹ׳, end of quote. And see what I have written on the verse (Genesis 36:31): ״וְאֵלֶּה הַמְּלָכִים״."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:15.222194883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}